I have created my first branch and I have made some changes to the .gitignore file. I have added a line to ignore all .txt files and removed the line that was ignoring two.txt file.
Now, I want to commit these changes to my branch. I will use the following commands:
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Updated .gitignore to ignore all .txt files and removed two.txt from ignore list"
After committing the changes, I will push the branch to the remote repository using:
git push origin Branch_1
This will allow me to share my changes with others and also create a pull request later to merge my branch into the main branch.    
